Personal AI Monitor

Personal AI Monitor is a local-first macOS personal context recall project.

Runtime data, screenshots, OCR source text, logs, debug tokens, SQLite
databases, HA package caches, raw vault contents, and real activity records are
intentionally excluded from the repository and must not be redistributed.

The project must not be used to normalize hidden monitoring, employee
surveillance, classroom monitoring, or collection of another person's activity
without informed consent.

Public snapshot adaptations: bundled source-admission helpers with no private
configuration; generic owner fixtures; no personal memory catalogue or private
schedule registrations. The original AGPL-3.0-only terms continue to apply.
The Hermes-derived component retains its separate MIT license and provenance.

External domain-list data: no compiled Bloom snapshot is redistributed in this
public snapshot. The optional regeneration tool names StevenBlack/hosts,
blocklistproject/Lists, HaGeZi DNS Blocklists, and OISD as separate upstream
sources. Their own licenses govern any separately downloaded or rebuilt data.
Built-in local safeguards remain part of this project's source.
